Mark admin settings that have no effect on misskey-cf as unsupported (未対応).

These meta settings are accepted by admin/update-meta (and returned by admin/meta)
for upstream compatibility, but nothing on the Cloudflare stack reads them. The
admin UI keeps showing them, marked 未対応 (Japanese only) with the reason, and
no longer lets them be changed:

- Object storage (S3): drive files are always stored in R2. The page shows only
  the notice, and its menu entry is labelled 未対応.
- SMTP server: mail goes through Cloudflare Email Service; the SMTP fields are
  replaced by the notice ("enable email" and the sender address remain).
- Sensitive media detection: not implemented; the folder shows only the notice.
- Server machine stats: there is no machine to report; server-info is fixed.
- Charts for remote users / federated instances: charts are computed from the
  source tables on request, nothing is recorded.
- FTT per-timeline cache limits: timelines are read from PostgreSQL, there is no
  cache to cap (the FTT switch and its DB fallback still apply).
- Reactions buffering (RBT): reactions are always written immediately.

